10000 identical diodes in parallel behind 100 ohm, 51-point source sweep
* bench.id: perf_scal_parallel_diodes_dc_n10000
* bench.group: performance
* bench.title: 10000 identical diodes in parallel behind 100 ohm, 51-point source sweep
* bench.probes: v(a), i(v1)
* bench.tol.rel: 1e-6
* bench.tol.abs: 1e-9
* bench.expect: match
* bench.oracle: dc_nonlinear
* bench.ng.solver: both
* bench.timing: yes
* bench.size: 10000
* bench.est_rss_mib: 61
* bench.tags: nonlinear, dc, sweep, diode, jit_tier, devcount, family:perf_scal_parallel_diodes_dc
* bench.note: N=1e4 identical diodes, same circuit and sweep as the 1e3 member so any growth of the time is the device count; mpmath oracle: rustspice max error 3.0e-11 V; measured on an idle core: rustspice e2e 91 ms (solve 80 ms, VmHWM 13 MiB) vs ngspice SPARSE 206 ms (solve 149 ms, 40 MiB) and KLU 218 ms
